# Knowledge Base Maintenance

The `knowledge/` folder is the system of record for this codebase. It lives
alongside `AGENTS.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` at the repository root.

> Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`knowledge/product-specs/index.md`](../../knowledge/product-specs/index.md) at the start of any non-trivial task.

## When to update

Update the knowledge base when you:

1. Add a new feature → create a spec in `knowledge/product-specs/` using
   [`knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md`](../../knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md)
   and add it to the index.
2. Change an existing feature's data model, API shape, tier gating, or telemetry
   → edit its spec.
3. Add or change a DB table, cron job, or feature flag → run
   `npm run knowledge:gen` and commit the resulting changes under
   `knowledge/generated/`.
4. Introduce an architectural pattern worth preserving → add a design doc at
   `knowledge/design-docs/<slug>.md`.
5. Change `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/rules/` → cross-link the relevant spec
   to the updated skill or rule.

## Required sections

Every product spec must contain the numbered sections from
[`knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md`](../../knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md).
The linter (`npm run knowledge:lint`) warns on missing sections.

## Do not edit

Files under `knowledge/generated/` are produced by `npm run knowledge:gen`.
Edit the source (migrations, cron registry, skills) instead.

## CI

`.github/workflows/knowledge-lint.yml` runs on every push:

- `npm run knowledge:lint` (broken links fail CI).
- `npm run knowledge:gen` — any drift fails CI with the diff.

## When in doubt

Link instead of inlining. The knowledge base works because it's a graph, not a
single document.
